21:["$","section","1-How to read an Italian tuition figure",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-2","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to read an Italian tuition figure"}],[["$","p","A single number rarely describes every student. The payable amount can depend on the programme, ECTS load, family economic indicator, foreign-income documentation, citizenship or residence category and any exemption. Application fees, regional tax, stamp duty and insurance can sit outside an advertised tuition waiver.",{"children":"A single number rarely describes every student. The payable amount can depend on the programme, ECTS load, family economic indicator, foreign-income documentation, citizenship or residence category and any exemption. Application fees, regional tax, stamp duty and insurance can sit outside an advertised tuition waiver."}],["$","p","The figures below come from official pages for 2026–2027 and provide a comparison method. Confirm the exact programme and your assessed amount before accepting an offer.",{"children":"The figures below come from official pages for 2026–2027 and provide a comparison method. Confirm the exact programme and your assessed amount before accepting an offer."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
22:["$","section","2-University of Padua",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"University of Padua"}],[["$","p","For 2026–2027, Padua lists fixed all-inclusive contributions of €2,790 for Group A and €2,990 for Group B for extra-EU students whose household is not resident in Italy. Other categories and specific reduced-country contributions exist; the minimum advertised fee is not every student's bill.",{"children":"For 2026–2027, Padua lists fixed all-inclusive contributions of €2,790 for Group A and €2,990 for Group B for extra-EU students whose household is not resident in Italy. Other categories and specific reduced-country contributions exist; the minimum advertised fee is not every student's bill."}],["$","p","Check the exact programme, household-residence category, mandatory charges and waiver exclusions. These figures are a labelled historical reference, not confirmed 2027–2028 fees. The university profile links the current fee page and explains how to track future award notices.",{"children":"Check the exact programme, household-residence category, mandatory charges and waiver exclusions. These figures are a labelled historical reference, not confirmed 2027–2028 fees. The university profile links the current fee page and explains how to track future award notices."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","nav",null,{"className":"answer-links","aria-label":"Next steps for University of Padua","children":[["$","$L4","/guides/university-of-padua-admissions-scholarships/",{"href":"/guides/university-of-padua-admissions-scholarships/","children":["Padua admission, fee categories and scholarships",["$","$L5",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$12:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}]]}]]}]
23:["$","section","3-Politecnico di Milano",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Politecnico di Milano"}],[["$","p","For a standard 46–74 ECTS study plan, Polimi publishes an annual amount from €157.04 up to €3,943.04 according to economic and study-plan conditions. Its 2026–2027 page states a first enrolment instalment of €880.04, with possible reduction through the stated ISEE process, and a later second instalment based on the relevant assessment.",{"children":"For a standard 46–74 ECTS study plan, Polimi publishes an annual amount from €157.04 up to €3,943.04 according to economic and study-plan conditions. Its 2026–2027 page states a first enrolment instalment of €880.04, with possible reduction through the stated ISEE process, and a later second instalment based on the relevant assessment."}],["$","p","Reserved non-EU master's students admitted with a foreign first degree who do not receive a qualifying scholarship are charged the maximum according to the study-plan percentage under the published rule. Merit scholarships can provide a full tuition waiver and some include an allowance, while DSU follows a separate economic and merit process.",{"children":"Reserved non-EU master's students admitted with a foreign first degree who do not receive a qualifying scholarship are charged the maximum according to the study-plan percentage under the published rule. Merit scholarships can provide a full tuition waiver and some include an allowance, while DSU follows a separate economic and merit process."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Published standard annual range: €157.04 to €3,943.04",{"children":"Published standard annual range: €157.04 to €3,943.04"}],["$","li","2026–2027 first instalment stated as €880.04 before an applicable reduction",{"children":"2026–2027 first instalment stated as €880.04 before an applicable reduction"}],["$","li","Foreign-income students may need Equalised ISEEU",{"children":"Foreign-income students may need Equalised ISEEU"}],["$","li","Check merit and DSU applications separately",{"children":"Check merit and DSU applications separately"}]]}],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
24:["$","section","4-University of Bologna",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"University of Bologna"}],[["$","p","Bologna describes its fee as a fixed €157.04 instalment plus a variable contribution based on the degree programme and the family's economic situation. The maximum varies by programme. Applicants who do not submit the required ISEE or foreign-income documents can be charged the full programme amount.",{"children":"Bologna describes its fee as a fixed €157.04 instalment plus a variable contribution based on the degree programme and the family's economic situation. The maximum varies by programme. Applicants who do not submit the required ISEE or foreign-income documents can be charged the full programme amount."}],["$","p","For 2026–2027, the university listed the first instalment by 24 September 2026, followed by possible instalments on 18 December 2026 and 15 March 2027. A degree can set a different first deadline. ER.GO scholarship and accommodation applications use their own calendar.",{"children":"For 2026–2027, the university listed the first instalment by 24 September 2026, followed by possible instalments on 18 December 2026 and 15 March 2027. A degree can set a different first deadline. ER.GO scholarship and accommodation applications use their own calendar."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Fixed component: €157.04",{"children":"Fixed component: €157.04"}],["$","li","Variable amount: programme and economic assessment",{"children":"Variable amount: programme and economic assessment"}],["$","li","Foreign-income documents affect reductions",{"children":"Foreign-income documents affect reductions"}],["$","li","ER.GO and university fee deadlines must both be tracked",{"children":"ER.GO and university fee deadlines must both be tracked"}]]}],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
25:["$","section","5-Compare the net annual cost",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Compare the net annual cost"}],[["$","p","For each university, start with the maximum amount applicable to your category. Subtract only a confirmed waiver or award, then add mandatory charges, housing, food, transport, insurance, residence-permit costs, travel and study materials. Keep the first-year arrival budget separate from the later annual budget.",{"children":"For each university, start with the maximum amount applicable to your category. Subtract only a confirmed waiver or award, then add mandatory charges, housing, food, transport, insurance, residence-permit costs, travel and study materials. Keep the first-year arrival budget separate from the later annual budget."}],["$","p","A lower tuition figure can be outweighed by a higher housing cost, while a large scholarship can arrive after deposits are due. Compare the timing of cash as well as the annual total.",{"children":"A lower tuition figure can be outweighed by a higher housing cost, while a large scholarship can arrive after deposits are due. Compare the timing of cash as well as the annual total."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
26:["$","section","6-A university comparison worksheet",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-7","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"A university comparison worksheet"}],[["$","p","Record one answer and one official URL for every field. A blank answer is a research task, not permission to assume zero.",{"children":"Record one answer and one official URL for every field. A blank answer is a research task, not permission to assume zero."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Degree and teaching language",{"children":"Degree and teaching language"}],["$","li","Admission and application fee",{"children":"Admission and application fee"}],["$","li","Maximum tuition for your category",{"children":"Maximum tuition for your category"}],["$","li","Economic-document deadline",{"children":"Economic-document deadline"}],["$","li","Mandatory regional and administrative charges",{"children":"Mandatory regional and administrative charges"}],["$","li","Merit scholarship",{"children":"Merit scholarship"}],["$","li","Regional DSU route",{"children":"Regional DSU route"}],["$","li","Estimated monthly housing",{"children":"Estimated monthly housing"}],["$","li","First payment date and scholarship payment date",{"children":"First payment date and scholarship payment date"}]]}],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
27:["$","section","7-Avoid misleading fee comparisons",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Avoid misleading fee comparisons"}],[["$","p","Do not compare one university's minimum subsidised figure with another university's maximum standard fee. Use the same applicant profile and study load. Distinguish a tuition waiver from a cash scholarship and label every figure with its academic year.",{"children":"Do not compare one university's minimum subsidised figure with another university's maximum standard fee. Use the same applicant profile and study load. Distinguish a tuition waiver from a cash scholarship and label every figure with its academic year."}],["$","p","Before paying, reopen the official fee notice from the university account or degree page. A third-party article cannot calculate your final bill.",{"children":"Before paying, reopen the official fee notice from the university account or degree page. A third-party article cannot calculate your final bill."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
28:["$","section",null,{"className":"source-section","aria-labelledby":"official-sources","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"official-sources","children":"Official sources and verification"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Source records support the guide. Page update dates describe editorial changes; they do not mean every linked rule was checked again today. Reopen the current call for your programme and intake."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"source-grid","children":[["$","$L4","https://www.unipd.it/en/contribuzione-studentesca",{"href":"https://www.unipd.it/en/contribuzione-studentesca","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"University of Padua: student fees"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Official 2026–2027 fees and exemptions"}]]}],["$","$L5",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M15 3h6v6","key":"1q9fwt"}],["path",{"d":"M10 14 21 3","key":"gplh6r"}],["path",{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6","key":"a6xqqp"}]],"className":"lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L4","https://www.unipd.it/en/borse-studio-agevolazioni-studenti-internazionali",{"href":"https://www.unipd.it/en/borse-studio-agevolazioni-studenti-internazionali","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"University of Padua: international scholarships"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Official award and fee-waiver routes"}]]}],["$","$L5",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$28:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L4","https://www.polimi.it/en/prospective-students/how-much-does-it-cost/laurea-laurea-magistrale-and-single-cycle-programmes",{"href":"https://www.polimi.it/en/prospective-students/how-much-does-it-cost/laurea-laurea-magistrale-and-single-cycle-programmes","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Politecnico di Milano: degree tuition fees"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Official annual fee range and 2026–2027 instalments"}]]}],["$","$L5",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$28:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L4","https://www.polimi.it/en/prospective-students/how-much-does-it-cost/scholarships",{"href":"https://www.polimi.it/en/prospective-students/how-much-does-it-cost/scholarships","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Politecnico di Milano: scholarships"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Official merit and DSU routes"}]]}],["$","$L5",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$28:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L4","https://www.unibo.it/en/study/enrolment-fees-and-other-procedures/degree-programmes/tuition-fees-and-exemptions",{"href":"https://www.unibo.it/en/study/enrolment-fees-and-other-procedures/degree-programmes/tuition-fees-and-exemptions","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"University of Bologna: tuition fees and exemptions"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Official components, foreign-income documents and 2026–2027 dates"}]]}],["$","$L5",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$28:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L4","https://www.unibo.it/en/study/study-grants-and-subsidies",{"href":"https://www.unibo.it/en/study/study-grants-and-subsidies","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"University of Bologna: grants and subsidies"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Official funding and regional-benefit routes"}]]}],["$","$L5",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$28:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L4","https://www.polimi.it/futuri-studenti/costi-e-borse-di-studio/corsi-di-laurea-laurea-magistrale-quinquennale-a-ciclo-unico",{"href":"https://www.polimi.it/futuri-studenti/costi-e-borse-di-studio/corsi-di-laurea-laurea-magistrale-quinquennale-a-ciclo-unico","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["$L2b","$L2c"]}]]}]]}]
29:["$","section",null,{"className":"faq-section","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Frequently asked questions"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","details","Which Italian university is cheapest for international students?",{"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":["Which Italian university is cheapest for international students?",["$","span",null,{"children":"+"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"There is no reliable answer without the programme and applicant profile. Compare the amount applicable to your category after economic assessment, then include mandatory charges and city living costs."}]]}],["$","details","Will I pay the minimum fee if my family income is low?",{"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":["Will I pay the minimum fee if my family income is low?",["$","span",null,{"children":"+"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Only if you meet the university's conditions and submit accepted economic documents by its deadline. Foreign income and assets may require a specific equivalent assessment."}]]}],["$","details","Does a full tuition waiver cover living costs?",{"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":["Does a full tuition waiver cover living costs?",["$","span",null,{"children":"+"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"No. A tuition waiver removes eligible tuition but normally does not pay housing, food, travel or every mandatory charge unless the award explicitly says so."}]]}],["$","details","Are application fees included in annual tuition?",{"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":["Are application fees included in annual tuition?",["$","span",null,{"children":"+"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Often they are separate and may be non-refundable. Check the admission page as well as the tuition page."}]]}]]}]]}]
